# L1 / B004 — package-management rule and architecture check script.

C R169 OL DEP-007 | MUST | Use npm for the frontend workspace unless the project deliberately adopts another package manager; keep package-lock.json consistent with package.json; place build/test tooling in devDependencies rather than runtime dependencies without a reason. | frontend packages | Deliberately adopted other package manager.
C U1 LU GOV-015,DEP-007 | MUST | Commit package.json and package-lock.json. | frontend workspace manifests | none stated | Read as a version-control content convention (both files belong in the repository) the clause is entailed by DEP-007; read as an instruction to perform commits it conflicts with GOV-015, which allows commits only on explicit request. The text does not resolve which reading is meant. | Under the commit reading an agent could commit lockfile changes without an explicit request; under the convention reading it only must not ignore or omit the lockfile.

